<title>BOTSWANA: AFRICAN COMMONWEALTH LEADERS TO MEET IN BOTSWANA.</title>
<headline>AFRICAN COMMONWEALTH LEADERS TO MEET IN BOTSWANA.</headline>
<dateline>GABORONE 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leaders of 18 African Commonwealth countries are due in the Botswana capital next Tuesday for two-day talks on democracy and good governance.</p>
<p>The meeting is due to start on February 26 in Kasane in the Chobe National Park, where the borders of Botswana, Zambia, Zimbabwe and Namibia converge.</p>
<p>Discussions will be chaired by Commonwealth secretary general Chief Emeka-Anyaoku.</p>
</text>
